 Tom Lee @fundstrat uses the  BS reason for today's drawdown  that there was a large forced liquidation to account for some of today's market decline.

Here is what Ken Griffin said on that lame excuse:

""Everyone's favorite go-to answer when they're losing money is hedge funds are de-leveraging... I've seen the entire industry de-leverage to zero at least 10,000 times"  Why it's dangerous:  "The reason that people love that answer is it actually washes your hands of accountability... the minute I start to use an excuse, I actually stop learning"  What he asks instead:  "What prices are changing and why? What don't we understand?... What dots have they connected that we don't see?"  His rule:  "That's like option 10 on the list, not option 1"
